Raspberry Pi Real-Time Transit Display

This project is used to track specific CTA bus and train routes but can be modified for other transit groups. For this project the following are required:
Raspberry Pi 3 or newer ( Pi 4B was used here)
7-inch display ( A 5-inch display would also work) [Amazon Link](https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0D3QB7X4Z?ref_=pe_148126100_1193965070_i_fed_asin_title&th=1)
An sd card and computer to flash the firmware.
Access to a 3D printer for the enclosure or use the provided stand.

Following the Raspberry Pi instructions download any of the standard operating systems for your device.
Create a URL for the ideal transit display from here. [CTA Bus Tracker Link] (https://www.transitchicago.com/developers/diybtform/)
Then using the file Kioskscreen create and add the URL before rebooting the device.


The 3d printed enclosure is meant to provide a durable case and a comfortable viewing angle from a desk or table. It can be printed with PLA and on any side with minimal supports.
Two versions of the enclosure exisit. One is meant to provide access to the GPIO pins while the other version is meant as a display only. A keyboard may be required to zoom in or out on the kiosk screen. 
